# Weylus Setup Complete!

I have installed **Weylus** to your system and successfully configured the system rules (`uinput`) to allow it to receive Apple Pencil pressure data.

Additionally, I've created a desktop shortcut for Weylus. This means you can easily search for "Weylus" in your app menu to start it when you need it, and simply close the app when you're done!

> [!WARNING]
> **RESTART REQUIRED!**
> Because I added your user account to the new `uinput` group, you **must** reboot your computer for the system permissions to take effect. If you skip this, your Apple Pencil pressure won't work!

---

## How to Connect over USB

You mentioned wanting this to work over USB. Because your system already has `usbmuxd` installed (the daemon that handles iOS USB communication), **Weylus supports this out-of-the-box!**

**Steps to use over USB:**
1. Connect your iPad to your laptop using a USB cable. 
   *(Make sure you unlock your iPad and tap "Trust this Computer" if prompted)*
2. Launch **Weylus** from your application menu on your laptop.
3. Click the **"Start"** button in Weylus.
4. On your iPad, open **Safari** (it *must* be Safari, other browsers won't work well) and navigate to: `http://localhost:1701`
5. You should now see your computer screen on your iPad!

---

## How to *Extend* Your Screen (Wayland)

Currently, Weylus will *mirror* whatever screen it captures. Because you are using Wayland, the system does not allow applications to easily "fake" a second monitor to extend into.

To get an extended screen setup, you will need to create a **Virtual Monitor**. The easiest way to do this on your setup is using a GNOME Shell Extension.

1. Install the Extension Manager app (if you don't have it):
   ```bash
   sudo apt install gnome-shell-extension-manager
   ```
2. Open **Extension Manager** and search for: **Virtual Monitors** (by *AlynxZhou*).
3. Install the extension. 
4. Once installed, you will have a new icon in your top bar. Click it to create a Virtual Monitor.
5. In the Weylus app on your laptop, select the newly created virtual monitor from the "Screen" dropdown before clicking Start!

> [!TIP]
> Make sure to check **"Enable Uinput"** in the Weylus interface to enable Apple Pencil pressure mapping!
